# ElimuTrack Teacher API

Reference for the Google AI Studio teacher app. The abandoned `teacher-mobile/`
app is not part of this integration.

## 1. Connection

| Environment | API base URL |
| --- | --- |
| Production | `https://site-4457d1964dd64e19ba7fec208a2066ee.freebuff.page` |
| Preview | `https://site-5f778f268f6643adacf08da7104b6e48.freebuff.page` |

Every endpoint below is under `/api`. All request and response bodies are JSON
(`Content-Type: application/json`), except `/api/broadsheet/csv`, which returns a
CSV download.

Use production unless you are explicitly testing preview data.

### CORS and authentication model

The Worker now accepts either:

1. **Bearer token (use this from AI Studio):**
   `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every request after login.
2. **Same-origin cookie:** the `elmt_staff` cookie used by the web app.

`POST /api/auth/login` returns the bearer token in the response body as `token`.
Use `credentials: "omit"` for cross-origin requests. Do **not** use
`credentials: "include"`: the API returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` for
token clients and deliberately does not allow credentialed cross-origin reads.

A token is valid for 7 days. Logging out revokes only that token. There is no
refresh endpoint; log in again when a request returns `401 UNAUTHENTICATED`.

### Minimal client setup

```js
const API = "https://site-4457d1964dd64e19ba7fec208a2066ee.freebuff.page";

let token = sessionStorage.getItem("elimutrack_token") || "";

async function api(path, options = {}) {
  const headers = {
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    ...(options.headers || {}),
  };
  if (token) headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;

  const response = await fetch(`${API}${path}`, {
    ...options,
    headers,
    credentials: "omit",
  });

  if (response.status === 401) {
    token = "";
    sessionStorage.removeItem("elimutrack_token");
    throw new Error("Session expired. Sign in again.");
  }

  if (!response.ok) {
    const problem = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));
    throw new Error(problem.error || `Request failed (${response.status})`);
  }

  return response.json();
}

async function login(username, password) {
  const session = await api("/api/auth/login", {
    method: "POST",
    body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }),
  });
  token = session.token;
  sessionStorage.setItem("elimutrack_token", token);
  return session;
}
```

Tokens must be kept out of URLs, logs and committed source. `sessionStorage`
keeps the teacher signed in for the current tab; use `localStorage` only if the
app should survive a full browser restart.

