## 3. Common response and error rules

Errors always look like:

```json
{
  "error": "Human-readable message",
  "code": "MACHINE_CODE"
}
```

| Status | Code | What the app should do |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `400` | `VALIDATION` | Show the message next to the form |
| `401` | `UNAUTHENTICATED` | Clear the token and open sign-in |
| `401` | `BAD_CREDENTIALS` | Show "wrong username or password" |
| `403` | `MUST_CHANGE_LOGIN` | Open the change-login screen |
| `403` | `SERVICE_DENIED` | Hide/disable that module; admin has not granted it |
| `403` | `OUT_OF_SCOPE` | Learner/class is outside the teacher's assigned streams |
| `403` | `FORBIDDEN` | Action is not allowed for this teacher |
| `404` | `NOT_FOUND` | Record no longer exists; refresh the list |
| `409` | `DUPLICATE_LESSON` | Scheme row already exists for that week/lesson |
| `409` | `DUPLICATE_ADMISSION` | Admission number already exists |
| `429` | `RATE_LIMITED` | Back off and retry later |

### Service gating

`session.services` is the authoritative list of modules the admin granted. A
teacher receives `403 SERVICE_DENIED` when calling an endpoint whose module is
not in that list. Apply the same rule in the UI: do not show a module the
teacher cannot use.

The API maps modules to endpoints as follows:

| Service | Endpoints |
| --- | --- |
| `learners` | `/api/learners` (also enabled if any roster service is granted) |
| `marks` | `/api/marks` |
| `attendance` | `/api/attendance` |
| `observations` | `/api/observations` |
| `fees` | `/api/payments` |
| `whatsapp` | `/api/whatsapp` |
| `schemes` | `/api/schemes`, `/api/schemes/bulk` |
| `lessonplans` | `/api/lesson-plans` |
| `recordwork` | `/api/recordwork` |
| `progress` | `/api/progress` |
| `timetable` | `/api/timetable` |
| `dashboard` | `/api/dashboard` |
| `kicd` | `/api/kicd`, `/api/resources` |
| `broadsheet` | `/api/broadsheet/csv` |

`/api/learners` is the roster used by marks, attendance, progress and reports.
A teacher with only `marks` can still read the learner roster.

### Stream scope

A teacher only sees learners and records in `session.streams` (for example
`["Grade 7 Eta"]`). Always send `stream` exactly as it appears in that array.
`OUT_OF_SCOPE` means the selected learner or stream is not assigned to them.

### Subjects

Primary school:

| ID | Subject |
| --- | --- |
| `math_p` | Mathematics |
| `eng_p` | English |
| `kis_p` | Kiswahili |
| `env_p` | Environmental Activities |
