## 12. Progress

**Important:** this endpoint records a teacher's manual CBC stage and note. It
does **not** yet accept a rubric, descriptor level or numeric rubric score.

### `GET /api/progress?stream=Grade%207%20Eta&learner=lrn_123`

```json
{
  "records": [
    {
      "id": "prg_123",
      "learnerId": "lrn_123",
      "learnerName": "Amina Wanjiku",
      "stream": "Grade 7 Eta",
      "subjectId": "math",
      "day": "2026-11-16",
      "stage": "Developing",
      "note": "Needs more practice with place value.",
      "staffId": "stf_123",
      "author": "Alvin Ojiambo",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-16T08:00:00.000Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

### `POST /api/progress`

```json
{
  "learnerId": "lrn_123",
  "day": "2026-11-16",
  "stage": "Developing",
  "note": "Needs more practice with place value.",
  "subjectId": "math"
}
```

Required: `learnerId`, `day`, `stage`. `subjectId` and `note` are optional.
Allowed stages: `Beginning`, `Developing`, `Secure`, `Exceeding`.

Success `201`: `{ "record": { ...record } }`

### `DELETE /api/progress`

```json
{ "id": "prg_123" }
```

Success `200`: `{ "ok": true }`

The rubric-assessment workflow (sub-strand rubric, four levels, overall score)
is not implemented in this API yet. Do not invent a scoring formula in the AI
Studio app. The current supported workflow is the manual stage above.

