## 15. Curriculum designs and resources

### `GET /api/kicd?grade=Grade%207&subject=math`

`grade` is a display name (`Grade 1` ... `Grade 10`, plus PP1/PP2 where
available). `subject` accepts either the app ID (`math_p`, `eng`, `isci`) or a
name (`Mathematics`, `English`).

```json
{
  "levels": ["PP1", "PP2", "Grade 1"],
  "sources": [],
  "strands": ["Numbers", "Measurement"],
  "designs": [
    {
      "id": "kicd_123",
      "level": "Grade 7",
      "grade": "Grade 7",
      "subjectId": "math",
      "strand": "Numbers",
      "subStrand": "Place value",
      "outcomes": ["By the end of the sub-strand..."],
      "experiences": ["Learners to..."],
      "competencies": [],
      "standards": [],
      "inquiry": ["How do we...?"],
      "resources": ["Counters"],
      "assessment": ["Oral questions"],
      "inclusive": "",
      "origin": "kicd",
      "suggestedLessons": 4
    }
  ]
}
```

Use this to prefill schemes and lesson plans. The response can be large; cache
it per grade/subject and avoid requesting it on every screen.

### `GET /api/resources?grade=Grade%207&subject=math`

Returns the resource library filtered the same way. Resource records contain
`id`, `title`, `type`, `url`, `grade`, `subjectId`, `strand`, `subStrand` and
`description`.

